            </div>
            <div class="institution">North-West University (NWU) — 3rd Year</div>

            <p style="color: #475569; margin-bottom: 20px;">
                Currently pursuing a Bachelor of Science in Information Technology, focusing on software engineering principles, decision support systems, mathematical optimization models, operating systems, and relational database management.
            </p>

            <div class="section-subtitle">Academic Focus & Key Competencies</div>
            <ul class="bullet-list">
                <li><strong>Operations Research & Optimization:</strong> Formulating linear programming (MILP) models to solve complex logistical and decision-making problems.</li>
                <li><strong>Relational Database Systems:</strong> Designing database architectures with Crow's Foot ERD modeling, referential integrity constraints, and complex SQL querying.</li>
                <li><strong>Software Engineering & Development:</strong> Developing robust software solutions using object-oriented principles across C++, Java, C#, and Python.</li>
